<!--frontend/about.ejs-->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style-about.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style-index.css">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" type="image/x-icon">
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet"
        integrity="sha384-QWTKZyjpPEjISv5WaRU9OFeRpok6YctnYmDr5pNlyT2bRjXh0JMhjY6hW+ALEwIH" crossorigin="anonymous">
    <title>
        Emergencies
    </title>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="topnav">
        <a class="active" href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="about">About</a>
        <a href="register">Register</a>
        <div class="login-btn">
            <button onclick="document.getElementById('id01').style.display='block'" class="login-btn">Login</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="id01" class="modal">
        <form action="/signin" method="post" class="modal-content animate" enctype="application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
            autocomplete="off">
            <div class="imgcontainer">
                <span onclick="document.getElementById('id01').style.display='none'" class="close"
                    title="Close">&times;</span>
                <img src="/img/login.jpg" alt="Avatar" style="width:75px; height:75px;">
            </div>

            <div class="container">
                <div class="input-group">
                    <input type="text" placeholder="Enter Username" name="username" id="username" autocomplete="off"
                        required>
                    <span class="error" id="usernameError"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="input-group">
                    <input type="password" placeholder="Enter Password" name="psw" id="psw" autocomplete="off" required>
                    <span class="error" id="passwordError"></span>
                </div>
                <button type="submit" class="popup-login-btn">Login</button>

            </div>
            <hr>
            <div class="container">
                <button type="button" onclick="document.getElementById('id01').style.display='none'"
                    class="cancelbtn">Cancel</button>
                <span class="psw">Forgot <a href="#">password?</a></span>
            </div>
        </form>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-section">
        <h1>A Little Something</h1>
        <p>If you want to be comfortable at home.</p>
        <p>Stop looking out the window, Look within.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="text-align:center">Babak Milani</h2>
    <div class="row">
        <div class="column">
            <div class="card">
                <img src="/img/babak.jpg" alt="Babak" style="width:20%; margin-bottom: 10px;">
                <div class="container">
                    <h2>Babak Milani</h2>
                    <p class="title">Software Engineering</p>
                    <p>This is a personal project I coded with MEN Stack in Visual Studio Code.</p>
                    <p>I build this project on Google Cloud because I used Google Maps API.</p>
                    <p>This is a web application for government agencies to register and</p>
                    <p>report emergencies in California. Emergencies can be found on</p>
                    <p>a map. The general public can signup to receive emails when a new</p>
                    <p>emergency is reported via email. The registered users can log in</p>
                    <p>report emergencies, find all there logs, and update the profile.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <div class="card">
                <div class="container">
                    <h2>Project Specs</h2>
                    <p class="title">MEN Stack : Mysql, ExpressJS, NodeJS, and Google Cloud</p>
                    <p>I developed a comprehensive and intricate project.
                        These components show a good understanding of Express.JS,
                    <p>middleware, authentication, database handling, and dynamic
                        content rendering, which are key elements in building a robust web application.</p>
                    <p><b>Use of Middleware and Sessions:</b> I used express-session and express-flash to manage
                        sessions
                        and display</br> flash messages, which adds complexity to the application.</p>
                    <p><b>User Authentication:</b> Implementing user authentication with bcrypt for password hashing and
                        checking</br> if users are authenticated before accessing certain routes.</p>
                    <p><b>Database Integration:</b> Connecting to a database and performing operations like querying
                        user
                        data.</p>
                    <p><b>Modular Architecture:</b> Well-structured with separate route files, making it
                        modular and easier to manage.</p>
                    <p><b>Error Handling and Redirection:</b> Managing errors and using flash messages to provide
                        feedback to
                        users.</p>
                    <p><b>Dynamic Content Rendering:</b> Using EJS to render dynamic content based on user data and
                        flash
                        messages.</p>
                    <p><button class="button">Contact</button></p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
        <p class="footer-txt">Developed by Babak Milani for employment purposes. All rights reserved 2024.</p>
    </div>
    <script src="/javascript/js.js"></script>
</body>

</html>